Package: MissingMediatorAnalysis
Type: Package
Title: Mediation Analysis with a Partially Missing Mediator and Outcome
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Haoyu", "Yang", email = "haoyuyang@hsph.harvard.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Product-of-coefficients mediation analysis when the mediator,
    and optionally the outcome, are partially missing at random given fully
    observed synthetic surrogates. SynMediation (sequential synthetic surrogate
    analysis) estimates both paths from three least-squares fits that use all
    subjects through the surrogates. Weighted SynMediation fits two of these
    regressions with inverse probabilities of being observed, which makes the
    estimator target-preserving under missingness at random whatever the
    relation between the surrogates and the mediator and outcome; its
    validity then depends only on the missingness models, and with equal
    weights it reduces to SynMediation. Alternatives for the mediator-outcome
    path include the efficient augmented inverse probability weighted (AIPW)
    estimator of Qin, Zhang and Leung (2017) and its combination with
    complete-case regression. Inference on the indirect effect uses the
    stacked influence functions of both paths, so the cross-path covariance
    is accounted for. Binary outcomes (logistic outcome model) are handled by
    a target-preserving sequential augmented inverse probability weighted
    estimator: it estimates the full-cohort (complete-case) projections, and
    its validity depends only on the models for missingness, not on the
    surrogate or prediction models; weighted complete-case (IPW) and
    complete-case fits are also available.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: stats, utils, parallel, splines
